{
  "format": "evn-blocks",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "Robot: every block",
  "needs": "a robot: left wheel motor on port 4 (mounted mirrored), right on port 3, 62.4 mm wheels 170 mm apart, an EVN IMU on I2C port 3 fixed flat to the chassis, and 40 cm of clear floor ahead and 20 cm to each side. Keep the robot still while the program starts (the IMU settles in 8 to 25 s).",
  "description": "Every robot block once: set-up, straight, turn, both kinds of arc, driving at a speed, stopping, the speed and acceleration settings, the measurements, and the gyro. The moves go out and come back, so the robot ends near where it started.",
